                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 32,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hoik Chen",
                        "email": "hoik.chen.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "hoikchen-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry, this comment appears to have been removed by mistake."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I understand this wasn't used in this file so could be deleted, but ideally would have been a separate commit (no need to do this now though)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "Since this log would never be useful on any systems that don't implement /run/boot-device, would it be OK to just skip its creation if it doesn't exist?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hoik Chen",
                        "email": "hoik.chen.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "hoikchen-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @spinler@us.ibm.com,\nBased on this change (https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/90871), it seems that `Unknown` should be the default value.\n\nOr does IBM never have this path at all? If the path is never present on IBM systems, I can add a condition to skip it.\n\nIf we decide to skip it, are there any additional conditions you would like to add? For example, should we log an info, or should we simply skip it if the path `/run/boot-device` cannot be found?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "@spinler@us.ibm.com -\n\n1. Don't you want the RebootCause even if you don't have a way to identify the boot device?\n\n2. I implemented this for the static-norootfs layout but it should be pretty straight-forward for someone to add this file to the init scripts of other flash layouts.  I assume you have some level of redundancy in your boot device?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I looked at this more closely.\n1. I agree that the cause is more important than the boot device, so you can ignore comment.\n\nHaving actually look at discoverLastRebootCause for the first time, it does make me wonder if we don't really need the pinhole reset event that you had previously removed.\n\n@geissonator@yahoo.com do you think we should still emit that pinhole reset event if there's also a new RebootCause one that contains that info?\n\n2. Yea, we have redundancy, interesting idea to add that."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 279,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hoik Chen",
                        "email": "hoik.chen.wiwynn@gmail.com",
                        "username": "hoikchen-wiwynn"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @geissonator@yahoo.com,\nCould you please help review it when you have time?\nThank you!!"
                }
            ],
